      "teacher": [
       {
        "body": {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Establish the Testing Environment:",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "bullet_list",
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Say:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " Today you will demonstrate what you have learned during this investigation. Your goal is to show how well you can apply your reading and language skills to new passages about apprenticeship, craft, and learning.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "textColor",
                   "attrs": {
                    "color": "#208095"
                   }
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "TEI Format Guide",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "How to complete the TEI formats:",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "bullet_list",
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Multiple Choice (MC): ",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "For these items, choose the one answer that best matches the question. Read all four choices carefully before selecting your answer.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Fill-in-the-Blank (FITB):",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " For these items, you will write the word you hear on the line provided. Listen carefully as the word is read, then used in a sentence, then repeated. Spell the word as accurately as you can.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Multiple Select (MS):",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " \"For these items, there is more than one correct answer. The question will usually tell you to 'Select ",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "two",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "' or ask 'Which ",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": "three",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " statements...' If you only pick one, the item will not be fully correct.\"",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Sorting/Matching:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " \"You will see a list of details and two categories (Passage 1 and Passage 2). You must click and drag each detail into the correct box based on which author emphasized that point. Note: Some details might fit both, but choose the primary emphasis.\"",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Sequencing/Ordering:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " \"For the timeline or logical flow questions, you must drag the events into the correct chronological order as described in the text. Pay close attention to transition words like 'subsequently' or 'initially'.\"",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        "title": "Launch",
        "purpose": {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "The teacher will establish the testing environment for students to take their assessment.",
             "type": "text"
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        "audience": "teacher",
        "sequence": 1,
        "estimated_time_in_minutes": [
         5,
         5
        ]
       },
       {
        "body": {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Assessment Time!",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Provide students with access to the ",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "text": "Unit 2 Investigation 1 Assessment",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "text": " and walk them through the expectations.",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "Active Monitoring Notes",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "strong"
              },
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "attrs": {
            "align": null
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "text": "During the assessment, look for:",
             "type": "text",
             "marks": [
              {
               "type": "em"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "bullet_list",
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Multiple Select Troubleshooting:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " Watch for students who select only one response on items that require two answers, or who do not notice directions such as “Select TWO details.”",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Spelling Administration:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " For the spelling items, maintain a neutral pace and follow the administration sequence exactly: read the word, read the sentence, repeat the word, and pause for students to write.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Pacing:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " Ensure students without extended time accommodations have moved into Passage 2 by the halfway mark (20 minutes), leaving enough time for the literary passage items and the spelling section.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Text Navigation:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " Watch for students who spend too long rereading entire passages instead of returning to specific paragraphs named in the item stems.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "list_item",
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Stem Interpretation:",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "strong"
                  },
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "text": " Monitor for students who appear stuck on academic wording such as central idea, theme, connotation, personification, or best supports. Redirect them to reread the stem carefully without paraphrasing toward an answer.",
                 "type": "text",
                 "marks": [
                  {
                   "type": "em"
                  }
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "collapsible",
           "attrs": {
            "label": "Integrated ELD Instructions"
           },
           "content": [
            {
             "type": "callout",
             "attrs": {
              "variant": "purpose"
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "To provide equitable access to complex literary texts and multi-step assessment items, ensuring that linguistic barriers do not impede a student's ability to demonstrate mastery of standards.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "For students requiring offline accommodations, provide a human reader. The reader must deliver the text, stems, and options at a measured, neutral pace without using inflection or tone to emphasize correct answers or suggest meaning.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "For students with Extended Time, provide a quiet transition for them to continue working while others move to the Look Back.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Focus facilitation on stems with dense academic wording, especially items asking students to identify what best supports an idea, how the author most effectively develops contrasting perspectives, or what a word most nearly means in context.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Encourage students to annotate passages in any language.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Affirm that English Learners bring cross-linguistic knowledge that supports comprehension of complex texts.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "type": "paragraph",
               "attrs": {
                "align": null
               },
               "content": [
                {
                 "text": "Remind students: You know more than you think. Trust your reading.",
                 "type": "text"
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "🛠️ TEACHER MOVES",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "strong"
                },
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "Allow students to point, gesture, or sketch to show a character’s shift in feeling or a contrast in perspective before answering.",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "Allow students to give a brief gist of the texts in their home language or in a mix of English and their home language to verify general understanding before they attempt items.",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "If a student is confused by the phrase ",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "text": "best supports",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "em"
                },
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "text": ", clarify that it means the detail that gives the strongest proof for the idea named in the question.",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "If a student is confused by the phrase ",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "text": "most nearly means",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "em"
                },
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "text": " ",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "text": "as it is used in the sentence",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "em"
                },
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              },
              {
               "text": ", clarify that they should use the context of that specific sentence, not just a memorized definition.",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "If a student is stuck on a prompt, ask them to whisper-read the prompt aloud. Hearing the language, especially complex syntax, often helps students decode the requirement.",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "Prompt: Tell me which words in the question matter most: character, theme, perspective, detail, or meaning. Start there.",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "Prompt: Before choosing, say to yourself: What changed for this character, and which line or detail proves it?",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "paragraph",
             "attrs": {
              "align": null
             },
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "If a student's written response or oral clarification includes dialectal variations, validate the linguistic diversity as a transferable skill.",
               "type": "text",
               "marks": [
                {
                 "type": "textColor",
                 "attrs": {
                  "color": "#bf360c"
                 }
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
